# config/axes/Kconfig.use — The USE axis (what the image is for), derived from PRESET
#
# The USE axis is derived from PRESET, never chosen: each USE_* symbol is a
# `def_bool PRESET_<same>` with no prompt, so `make config` shows the Preset
# menu only, and a defconfig line that sets a USE_* symbol is ignored
# (olddefconfig recomputes it); HWCLASS, STRUCTURE, RT, SECURITY and VIRT stay
# visible as overrides. A preset gets a USE_* symbol only when something reads
# it (a default, an `imply`, a cargo feature or the code):
# PRESET_FIRMWARE has none, as nothing depends on it
# (tools/kconfig_lint.py: every symbol has a reader). AZOS is a general-purpose hybrid kernel; a robot is one worked
# example. USE decides which crates are linked (USE_ROBOT -> kernel feature
# `use-robot`, emitted by tools/kconfig_to_cargo.py), which menus `make
# config` shows, and, through `imply` and conditional defaults, the starting
# value of other options. It never forces one: every implied option can be
# changed by hand (wave 11).
#
# What each domain does:
#   Only Robot links the robot crates under domains/robot/ (behavior and the
#   brain link, safety-core, flight, the ESC and RC receiver drivers) plus the
#   IMU / barometer / GPS drivers. Every domain links the shared actuation
#   authority (crates/core/actuation: e-stop latch, signed release, flight
#   recorder, system watchdog). The other domains change defaults only, with
#   `imply` or a conditional default, never `select`.

config USE_GENERIC
    def_bool PRESET_GENERIC
    help
      A general-purpose kernel: scheduler, IPC, file
      systems, network, drivers, ring-3 services, and the shared
      actuation authority (e-stop latch, flight recorder, sys-wdt).
      No robot crate is linked and no robot task is started: built
      with `--no-default-features` plus the rest of the kernel's
      default features (tools/kconfig_to_cargo.py).

config USE_ROBOT
    # cargo-feature: use-robot base
    def_bool PRESET_ROBOT
    help
      Links the robot crates (kernel feature `use-robot`):
      behavior and the brain link, the motor control loop and the
      per-robot-type safety envelope (safety-core), IMU / barometer /
      GPS / AHRS, flight, navigation, telemetry, the in-kernel benches, and starts their tasks.
      Shows the "Robot" menu: robot type, brain link, the
      safety-layer timers and the motor control loop.

config USE_IOT_HMI
    def_bool PRESET_IOT_HMI
    imply DRV_DISPLAY_HDMI if !HWCLASS_EMBEDDED
    imply DRV_DISPLAY_RAMFB if !HWCLASS_EMBEDDED
    help
      Devices with a display, touch input and a battery. Implies
      (default on, can be turned off under "Drivers"): the display
      driver of the board (DRV_DISPLAY_HDMI on the VF2,
      DRV_DISPLAY_RAMFB on QEMU riscv64; neither exists elsewhere).
      Not implied on a small board (HWCLASS_EMBEDDED): its defconfig names the drivers its
      topology starts. The INA219 /
      ADS1115 drivers that read a supply voltage and current are in
      every image. There is no touch-controller driver in the tree.
      The battery's state of charge is estimated by the power service
      (POWER.ELF) from the INA219's samples, and the topology's
      [degrade.NAME] rows choose the degrade level for it.

config USE_GATEWAY
    def_bool PRESET_GATEWAY
    help
      A node that aggregates many downstream devices. On the Edge
      deployment profile it changes the network defaults (each can be
      set by hand under "Resource Limits" / "Network"):
        TCP_MAX_CONNS 8 -> 64, TCP_BUF_SIZE 131072 -> 16384:
          64 x 38,904 B = 2,489,856 B of TCP tables, against
          8 x 268,280 B = 2,146,240 B on Edge (+343,616 B);
        MAX_SOCKETS 16 -> 128 (+112 UDP-sized slots);
        ARP_CACHE_SIZE 16 -> 64, ARP_PENDING_SIZE 8 -> 16,
        DNS_CACHE_SIZE 4 -> 16, UDP_RX_SLOTS 4 -> 16.
      Smaller per-connection buffers for many more connections: a
      gateway holds many mostly idle links, not a few bulk ones.
      The Fleet profile (HWCLASS_SERVER) keeps its own, larger tables.

config USE_INDUSTRIAL
    def_bool PRESET_INDUSTRIAL
    help
      Control equipment with timing and fault-containment needs.
      Mmap commits at map time (MM_DEMAND_PAGING starts off). The
      threat model is the SECURITY posture (PRESET_INDUSTRIAL sets
      separation-static, the physical-access one: "Physical access to the
      device"). Existing pieces: the CAN
      driver (crates/drivers/bus/src/can.rs), the control-loop
      rollback (CONTROL_TXN_TICKS) under "Scheduling, IPC & timing".
      The fair class is EEVDF; bounded latency comes from the RT band
      and the DL class (no deadline scheduler runs in a default image).

config USE_AUTOMOTIVE
    def_bool PRESET_AUTOMOTIVE
    help
      Vehicle electronics with timing and fault-containment needs.
      As Industrial it commits mmap at map time (MM_DEMAND_PAGING
      starts off); the CAN driver and the control-loop rollback listed
      under "Industrial" are its existing pieces.

config USE_DESKTOP
    def_bool PRESET_DESKTOP
    help
      An interactive machine with a display and input. Today it
      changes no default beyond what PRESET_DESKTOP sets on the other
      axes.

config USE_SERVER
    def_bool PRESET_SERVER
    help
      A machine serving many clients. Today it changes no default
      beyond what PRESET_SERVER sets on the other axes (the Fleet
      tables come from HWCLASS_SERVER).

config USE_WEARABLE
    def_bool PRESET_WEARABLE
    help
      An energy-first device (watch, band). Today it changes no
      default beyond what PRESET_WEARABLE sets on the other axes.
